Your leadership in infrastructure and Nokia's evolution from a pulp mill to a global connectivity leader in the AI era is truly inspiring. I hope to bring that same level of adaptability to the team as I transition from a career in financial data analysis into software development.

My journey into engineering began at Hive in 2025, where I discovered my passion for solving problems with code. From learning low level concepts such as memory management and bit manipulation to collaborating with my peers to solve a bug we both encountered, I've developed my skills as a well-rounded coder in a fast pace, intensive learning environment.

My favorite project had been building a interactive shell interpreter with a fellow Hiver. We got to learn system programming while strengthening our communication and collaboration. The thing I've enjoyed the most was learning to work with git in a team setting. Going through bugs and solving merge conflicts with my partner was the highlight of the project for me. I also took the lead on writing unit tests for our lexical analysis component, which used linked lists under the hood. Having that test coverage meant we could iterate confidently without worrying about quietly breaking something unexpected.

Before Hive, I spent several years working as Senior Data Analyst at Financial Recovery Technologies helping institutional clients recover money from class action lawsuits. The role required me to work with large volume of trading data to spot anomalies and patterns early and communicate effectively to different stakeholders. I've learn to speak the language that different people use to explain what the data is telling. I became efficient in translating technical requirements to business needs for clients.

Beyond my professional life, I am an avid runner with seven marathons and many other shorter distance races under my belt. It helps me to stay healthy physically and gives me a sense of resilience when facing discomfort.

I look forward to bringing my attention to details, communication skills, resilience and curiosity to #company. Thank you for your time and consideration.

Sincerely,

#author
